From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 192/488] soh: rename D_8016B6C0 -> gUnusedFaultDrawerBuffer

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence GUESS) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: char[0x20] declared right after sFaultDrawerStruct with no reader anywhere; size suggests a scratch print buffer, which is why it is named a buffer, but nothing confirms the use.
Defined in soh/src/code/fault_drawer.c.

Tagged [LLM:GUESS] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 soh/src/code/fault_drawer.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/fault_drawer.c b/soh/src/code/fault_drawer.c
index 8cd08248f..debac842d 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/fault_drawer.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/fault_drawer.c
@@ -70,7 +70,8 @@ FaultDrawer sFaultDrawerDefault = {
 };
 
 FaultDrawer sFaultDrawerStruct;
-char D_8016B6C0[0x20];
+// LLM generated name (GUESS), was D_8016B6C0: char[0x20] declared right after sFaultDrawerStruct with no reader anywhere; size suggests a scratch print buffer, which is why it is named a buffer, but nothing confirms the use.
+char gUnusedFaultDrawerBuffer[0x20];  // was D_8016B6C0 [LLM:GUESS]
 
 void FaultDrawer_SetOsSyncPrintfEnabled(u32 enabled) {
     sFaultDrawerStruct.osSyncPrintfEnabled = enabled;
